{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"length","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"","reasoning_content":"We have CNF with 12 variables, 12 clauses. Need count of assignments satisfying all clauses. Use enumeration? 2^12=4096 manageable. But we can use tool enumerate? There's tool enumerate but may be heavy. We can use brute force logic manually? Let's analyze constraints.\n\nClauses list:\n\n1. [1,10] => x1 OR x10\n2. [7,5] => x7 OR x5\n3. [-2,11] => ¬x2 OR x11\n4. [4,3] => x4 OR x3\n5. [-10,9] => ¬x10 OR x9\n6. [6,2] => x6 OR x2\n7. [-1,9] => ¬x1 OR x9\n8. [-6,11] => ¬x6 OR x11\n9. [-3,8] => ¬x3 OR x8\n10. [-7,12] => ¬x7 OR x12\n11. [-4,8] => ¬x4 OR x8\n12. [-5,12] => ¬x5 OR x12\n\nWe need count assignments satisfying all.\n\nWe can attempt to derive constraints.\n\nLet's denote variables: x1..x12.\n\nClause 1: x1 ∨ x10. So at least one of x1,x10 true.\n\nClause 7: ¬x1 ∨ x9 => x1 -> x9. Equivalent: if x1 true then x9 true. Also if x9 false then x1 false.\n\nClause 5: ¬x10 ∨ x9 => x10 -> x9. So both x1 and x10 imply x9.\n\nClause 3: ¬x2 ∨ x11 => x2 -> x11. Also if x11 false then x2 false.\n\nClause 8: ¬x6 ∨ x11 => x6 -> x11. So x6 also implies x11.\n\nClause 6: x6 ∨ x2 => at least one of x6,x2 true.\n\nThus from 6, either x6 true or x2 true (or both). Both imply x11 true. So x11 must be true if either x6 or x2 true. But could both be false? No, because clause 6 requires at least one true. So at least one of x6,x2 true. Therefore x11 must be true. So x11 is forced true. Good.\n\nThus x11=1.\n\nNow clause 3 and 8 satisfied automatically because x11 true.\n\nNow consider variables x7,x5,x12.\n\nClause 2: x7 ∨ x5. So at least one of x7,x5 true.\n\nClause 10: ¬x7 ∨ x12 => x7 -> x12. So if x7 true then x12 true.\n\nClause 12: ¬x5 ∨ x12 => x5 -> x12. So if x5 true then x12 true.\n\nThus at least one of x7,x5 true, and whichever true forces x12 true. So x12 must be true if either x7 or x5 true. Since at least one is true, x12 must be true. So x12=1.\n\nThus x12 forced true.\n\nNow consider x4,x3,x8.\n\nClause 4: x4 ∨ x3. So at least one of x4,x3 true.\n\nClause 9: ¬x3 ∨ x8 => x3 -> x8. So if x3 true then x8 true.\n\nClause 11: ¬x4 ∨ x8"}}],"created":1790943012,"model":"C:\\Users\\d2j3\\Documents\\Codex\\2026-09-10\\napraw\\outputs\\moon-native\\models\\gpt-oss-20b-MXFP4.gguf","system_fingerprint":"b10809-5266f24da","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":768,"prompt_tokens":4196,"total_tokens":4964,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-UdWueUbvQOjySnI50cea0sb4Ljuf5jdm","timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":4196,"prompt_ms":564.258,"prompt_per_token_ms":0.13447521448999047,"prompt_per_second":7436.314593678778,"predicted_n":768,"predicted_ms":2388.801,"predicted_per_token_ms":3.1144732724902218,"predicted_per_second":321.08158025720854}}